      "id": "AX-PR-T47-06-T47.06.a-DELAYED",
      "author_readiness": "ready-bounded",
      "demonstration": "Actual two-slot copied snapshot retention composes SlSnapshot under a hub mutex, publishes exact owner/slot/nonwrapping serial and preserves versions across later commits, source poison and close. MAX retires only after cleanup; stale/double release cannot consume a reused slot. Close retains readers until release, with joined callers required before mutex destruction. The contract/analysis explicitly derives additional root/page-version/reader-registration/reclamation machinery a zero-copy design would need. This is implemented full-copy retention, not a claim of page-level MVCC.",
